34,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems we must be cautious. Our development budget is tighter than usual, and I've noticed that only on-site sessions generate revenue. We should prioritize programs that are financially viable and don't drain our limited funds.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Financial viability is one thing, but efficacy is another. My research shows that while some outreach can reduce readmissions, physical visits are often unreliable due to external factors. We shouldn't invest in a flawed delivery model.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm quite concerned about our staffing. We have significant nursing vacancies and a loss of physiotherapists, though the midwifery rota actually has some unusual slack. We must choose a program that doesn't overburden our exhausted teams.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm worried too! Our rooms and parking fill up so fast, and the shuttle doesn't reach most villages. Also, if a program doesn't have fixed appointments, the booking system won't even record the work!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is so important to be mindful of these things. I found that joint ventures can struggle when responsibilities aren't clear, and agreements with outside surgeries can take a very long time to finalize.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, it is interesting that the midwifery rota has slack. Given the budget constraints and the fact that on-site work is the only way to secure funding, perhaps a program utilizing that capacity would be wise.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, focusing on available capacity is logical, but we must ensure the program is actually measurable. If it doesn't fit the booking system, as @Kenji mentioned, it will just be another buried initiative.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, I agree that using the midwifery slack would be a balanced approach. It would allow us to start something new without adding pressure to the nursing wards, which are already struggling with vacancies.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shion, that's a great point! If we pick something that uses the booking system's fixed slots, we can actually prove it's working. But we still have to figure out how people will get here!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, you are so right to worry about the travel. We must be careful not to create a service that is too difficult for our dear patients to reach, or one that relies on outside signatures.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, your point about outside signatures is crucial. If we avoid external dependencies and focus on on-site services using existing slack, we can ensure the program is both funded and manageable.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Midori, @Jonathan, it seems we are converging on a solution that utilizes the midwifery slack and remains on-site. This avoids the unreliability of home visits and the bureaucracy of external agreements.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I agree. A program that leverages the midwifery team's current capacity while staying on-site would maintain harmony across the departments and avoid adding stress to our nursing staff.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I agree! If we keep it on-site and use the booking system, we can track everything. I just hope we can find a way to manage the parking and shuttle issues for the patients!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, your kindness for the patients is heartwarming. If we choose a program that is well-organized and on-site, we can at least ensure the care is stable and the staff are happy.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems we have a shared understanding. We need a program that is on-site for funding, utilizes existing staffing slack to avoid burnout, and fits our booking system for accountability. I look forward to seeing the candidates.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Indeed. We must avoid the trap of idealistic programs that vanish from the records. A logical choice will be one that is measurable, sustainable, and doesn't rely on the unpredictability of external partners or home visits.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree with everyone. Let's hope the candidates include something that supports our patients while respecting the limits of our staff and facilities. I'm ready to see the options.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm ready too! I'll be cheering for the option that makes the most sense for our space and our patients. Let's see what the candidates are!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree with you all. It is a comfort to see such a thoughtful consensus. Let us hope we find a program that brings peace and healing to our community without burdening our dear staff.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
