59,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Looking at the options, Candidate C is the most sustainable. It utilizes the midwifery slack @Midori mentioned, stays on-site for funding, and uses scheduled slots for the booking system. It avoids the risks we discussed.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, I agree. Candidate A and D rely on the external factors and data agreements we've already flagged as problematic. Candidate B is impossible given the physiotherapy staffing shortage. C is the only logical, measurable choice.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,I completely agree. Candidate C aligns perfectly with the midwifery capacity and avoids adding pressure to our nursing wards. It feels like the most balanced choice for both our patients and our staff.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Candidate C is the best! It uses scheduled slots so it won't disappear from the records, and since it's on-site, it's the most stable way to help our parents and babies. I vote for C!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is wonderful that we have found such a harmonious path. Candidate C avoids the pitfalls of joint budget disputes and external delays, ensuring our dear parents receive steady care. I also vote for C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
